<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Whip</h1>
<p>Average Length: 6 feet.
Type of weapon: Distanced Hand-to-Hand.
Commonly used by: Many classes.
</p><p>This was not a typical weapon, but it was fairly easy to come by. It was really a decent weapon, and could be used in a variety of ways (whipping, disabling an arm or leg, grabbing weapons, or as a rope). It could be cut easily by a sword, and it was hard to judge the distance for a snap while moving around, but it was pretty useful.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the whip is a weapon skill of its own, one of the special weapons (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): one-handed, it slashes, it leans on dexterity, with some strength, and it is quick, as light weapons are. No shield can stop a whip. It is taught by the assassins from guild level 9, the dark knights from guild level 9, the paladins from guild level 9, the rangers from guild level 9, the barbarians from guild level 9 (up to 70%), the fighters from guild level 9 (up to 60%) and the thieves from guild level 9 (up to 80%). Practising it needs dexterity 50.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
